+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | Draft                |
+
+The registry checks each tool call against the same JSON Schema given to providers, so malformed model input becomes a useful tool result before an executor runs.
+
+## Contract
+
+- `ToolRegistry.execute` returns a `ToolResponse` naming a missing required property and does not invoke the executor; valid input, including unlisted properties, reaches the executor unchanged and exactly once ([validated by: rejects missing required input before execution and passes valid input through unchanged](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L4)).
+- A declared type or enum violation returns a result naming the property path and failed constraint without exposing the offending value ([validated by: reports type and enum failures by path and constraint without exposing input values](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L38)).
+- Registering a static tool with an uncompilable schema throws immediately and names the tool; a valid static schema is compiled at registration and reused across calls; an unknown tool name still throws `Unknown tool: <name>` ([validated by: rejects a broken static schema at registration and reuses a valid one](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L85)).
+- A function-valued definition is resolved for each call, and validation uses that call's schema rather than a previously resolved schema ([validated by: uses the current schema of a function-valued definition on each call](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L127)).
+- A rejected tool call is returned to the provider as a tool result so the provider can retry and `processMessage` resolves within the tool-round limit ([validated by: returns a rejected tool call to the provider for a corrected retry](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.acceptance.test.ts#L7)).
+
+Log lines name failing paths and constraints without revealing values.
+
+The registry does not forbid unlisted properties, coerce values, apply schema defaults, or offer a validation opt-out. `execute` has a one-line doc comment pointing to this contract. The validator is a runtime dependency so the published package imports successfully.
